From: LuneOS <webos-ports@googlegroups.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] browser_shell: deliver permission requests, add find-in-page,
 JavaScript and cookie switches

browser_shell apps had no way to ask any of this of the engine, so the browser
UI on LuneOS carried dead controls.

Permission requests: PageContents::RequestMediaAccessPermission handed the
dispatcher's answer straight back to the page, so the shell app was never
consulted. Everything needed for the round trip already existed -- the
media_access_requests_ map, AckPermission, the OnPermissionRequest delegate hook
and the "permissionrequest" event in the injection -- but nothing ever started
it, so the map stayed empty and AckPermission could only log "Not found
request". getUserMedia was therefore decided without the user, and enactbrowser's
own permissionrequest listener never fired once. The devices the dispatcher
picked are now held until the app answers; a request the dispatcher already
refused is passed straight through, since there is nothing to decide.

Find-in-page: exposes findInPage()/stopFindInPage() over WebContents::Find, with
results reported back on a new "found-in-page" event. Without it a browsershell
app can only fall back to window.find(), which cannot report a match count or
highlight the other matches.

setEnableJavascript / setAcceptCookies: pageContents exposed no web preferences
at all. JavaScript goes through OverrideWebkitPrefs, which is only consulted when
preferences are recomputed, hence the explicit NotifyPreferencesChanged. Cookies
go through the content settings map rather than the CookieManager directly, so
the change is not overwritten the next time the map syncs.

Upstream-Status: Pending
